DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI AutomationsListPage shipped at parity with the web source: an
@Observable AutomationsListPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injected
AutomationsListDataSource whose method names mirror the 8 ported web hooks verbatim
(useAutomations / useVehicles / usePinned / useAutomationHistory / useToggleAutomation /
useReEnableAutomation / useDeleteAutomation / useTestRunAutomation). The page reproduces the
web PageContainer chrome (title + subtitle + Import file-picker + Create), the four stat tiles,
the filters panel, the auto-disabled warning banner, the collapsible preset gallery, the
automation card list (with its no-data + no-match empty states), and the embedded execution
activity feed — built on the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel / TSCard / TSButton /
TSBadge / TSSelect / TSTextField / TSEmptyState / TSSkeleton / TSStaggerContainer / motion), no
hand-rolled glass; adaptive macOS/iPad vs iPhone-compact; every visible string from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; VoiceOver labels/traits + Dynamic Type + the
auto-disabled danger emphasis. Verified on BOTH idioms by real iOS-18 + macOS-15 Swift 6
strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0 on the surface) and an executed 26/26 model harness. The full
xcodebuild scheme is RED (BUILD_EXIT=65) ONLY due to the pre-existing, out-of-scope IRGen compiler
crash on AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift (forbidden to commit-fix) — the identical disposition
